__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
db/*.db
db/*.db-wal
db/*.db-shm
.venv/
.superpowers/

# Persistent OS-lock identities; never delete a lock file to unlock a writer.
theories/deadline_drift/data/.collector.lock
*.json.lock
**/.ticket-locks/

# SDD isolated worktrees
.worktrees/

# Daily floor reports are deliverables, not the record -- the audit
# trail is the DB, NOTES.md and RESEARCH_LOG.md, and a report is
# regenerable from the ledger. The folder README is tracked so the
# report's shape survives a fresh clone.
user_reports/*
!user_reports/README.md
# series-bias-mining: the collected corpus and its run artifacts.
# Ignored as a DIRECTORY, not one filename -- the -journal, the WAL
# and the per-run logs beside collect.db were all still untracked,
# so `git add -A` would have staged them. Regenerable via collect.py.
#
# Moved here 2026-09-02 from
# theories/insider_bias/mention_family/studies/investigation/, when
# mention_family was retired. The study was in flight and CLAUDE.md
# calls it infrastructure other studies read, so it became OWNERLESS
# rather than retiring with its theory -- retiring a theory must not
# retire a live measurement other work depends on. The 368MB under
# data/ is the part that could have been lost: Kalshi has aged that
# settled history out of its public API, so it is unrecoverable
# upstream and only "regenerable via collect.py" for the window that
# is still reachable.
#
# **Matched by STATE-INDEPENDENT glob, deliberately.** A study's state is
# the directory it sits in, so `cli tickets advance` MOVES this folder --
# and a path naming one state stops matching the moment it does. That is
# not hypothetical: parlay-markup below was advanced to `answer/` and its
# `investigation/`-pinned entry silently stopped covering a 17.6MB
# legs.db, leaving it untracked-and-unignored for the next `git add -A`
# to stage. Found 2026-09-03. The glob covers every state at once.
tickets/study/*/2026-08-29-series-bias-mining/data/
STATE.md

# parlay-markup study: 150k+ raw Kalshi leg payloads. NOT regenerable --
# this entry said "regenerable via collect.py" until 2026-09-03, and both
# halves of that stopped being true: the study reached its answer, so its
# investigation (collect.py included) was deleted, and re-collecting needs
# an API that drops settled markets ~60 days after close. Nothing in git
# holds this file either, which is why it is the one thing the answer
# sweep kept -- see the `**Retained:**` line in that study's STUDY.md.
tickets/study/*/2026-08-30-parlay-markup/data/

# taker_flow: the raw per-trade corpus for backtest-2026-09-01-takerflow
# (~5,200 markets, 305MB). Regenerable via backtest.collect(); the
# DERIVED decisions it produces are tracked beside it as decisions.json,
# which is what every analysis actually reads.
theories/taker_flow/backtests/settled_trades.jsonl

# News Drift source captures stay on disk; summaries/manifests remain searchable.
# These raw archives are local evidence, not a backup: API retention can expire.
theories/news_drift/backtests/*/raw/
theories/news_drift/backtests/*/history.db*

# Original weather captures are retained locally; compact manifests drive retrieval.
theories/weather_model_gap/backtests/*/raw/

# TSA source captures are retained locally; manifests identify their exact bytes.
theories/tsa_remainder_gap/backtests/*/raw/

# insider_judgment refresh runs: run-state.json is the price-bearing
# operator state (the whole board at run time, ~537MB on 2026-09-05) and
# must never reach git or a judge. The blind inputs, prompts, verdicts and
# receipts beside it are paid judgment source data and stay tracked.
theories/insider_bias/insider_judgment/runs/*/run-state.json
